# YBar integration for skhd — append to your ~/.config/skhd/skhdrc.
# A faithful translation of a real ~/.aerospace.toml's [mode.main.binding]
# and [mode.service.binding] into yabai/skhd equivalents. yabai's bsp/
# stack/float model isn't identical to AeroSpace's tiling tree, so a few
# bindings are the closest available analog rather than an exact match —
# called out inline. Mode transitions report to the bar's mode pill
# (widgets.skhd_mode), which AeroSpace's on-mode-changed hook doesn't have
# a YBar equivalent for otherwise.
#
# skhd's config is its own hotkey DSL, not shell — no variable assignment
# (a stray `ybar="..."` line here throws "undeclared identifier" and drops
# the rest of the file); every action spells out the literal path.
#
# CURRENT LIMITATION on this machine (confirmed by live testing, not
# assumed): `yabai -m space --focus`/`--display` need the scripting
# addition, which needs System Integrity Protection partially disabled.
# Bindings that call them are included and will start working the moment
# the scripting addition is installed — until then they're silent no-ops.
# Everything else below (focus, move/warp, resize, moving a window TO a
# space, floating, minimize) works today without it — verified live.

:: default    : /opt/homebrew/bin/ybar --trigger skhd_mode_changed MODE=default
:: service @  : /opt/homebrew/bin/ybar --trigger skhd_mode_changed MODE=service

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main mode

# Minimize the focused window and move focus to the next one in this space.
# (aerospace: custom cmd-m binding that manually minimized + walked the
# tiling tree to the next window — yabai's own --focus next replaces that
# whole dance.)
cmd - m : yabai -m window --minimize; yabai -m window --focus next

# Layout. Approximate: AeroSpace's "layout tiles horizontal vertical" /
# "layout accordion horizontal vertical" toggle a container's orientation
# and stacking within its own tree; yabai's bsp/stack are per-SPACE modes,
# not per-container, so these are the closest single-key equivalents.
# Key literals: this skhd build has NO named punctuation keys (verified
# against its own tokenizer source — only word keys like "escape"/"space"
# and arrows/f-keys/media keys exist) — every punctuation binding below
# uses the raw kVK_ANSI_* hex keycode instead (grammar: key = literal |
# keycode, keycode = apple kVK_<Key> hex value).
# 0x2C = kVK_ANSI_Slash, 0x2B = kVK_ANSI_Comma.
alt - 0x2C : yabai -m window --toggle split
alt - 0x2B : yabai -m space --layout $(yabai -m query --spaces --space | /usr/bin/python3 -c "import json,sys; print('bsp' if json.load(sys.stdin)['type']=='stack' else 'stack')")

# Focus.
alt - h : yabai -m window --focus west
alt - j : yabai -m window --focus south
alt - k : yabai -m window --focus north
alt - l : yabai -m window --focus east

# Move. (aerospace "move" == yabai "warp": re-insert the window at the
# target position.)
alt + shift - h : yabai -m window --warp west
alt + shift - j : yabai -m window --warp south
alt + shift - k : yabai -m window --warp north
alt + shift - l : yabai -m window --warp east

# Resize. Approximate: AeroSpace's "resize smart ±50" grows/shrinks the
# window along whichever axis makes sense for its position in the tree;
# yabai has no single-flag equivalent, so this resizes from the right edge.
# 0x1B = kVK_ANSI_Minus, 0x18 = kVK_ANSI_Equal.
alt - 0x1B : yabai -m window --resize right:-50:0
alt - 0x18 : yabai -m window --resize right:50:0

# Workspace switch. See the CURRENT LIMITATION note above — needs SA.
alt - 1 : yabai -m space --focus 1
alt - 2 : yabai -m space --focus 2
alt - 3 : yabai -m space --focus 3
alt - 4 : yabai -m space --focus 4
alt - 5 : yabai -m space --focus 5
alt - 6 : yabai -m space --focus 6
alt - 7 : yabai -m space --focus 7

# Move the focused window to a space WITHOUT following it (matches
# AeroSpace's move-node-to-workspace default). Verified live: works today,
# no SA needed.
alt + shift - 1 : yabai -m window --space 1
alt + shift - 2 : yabai -m window --space 2
alt + shift - 3 : yabai -m window --space 3
alt + shift - 4 : yabai -m window --space 4
alt + shift - 5 : yabai -m window --space 5
alt + shift - 6 : yabai -m window --space 6
alt + shift - 7 : yabai -m window --space 7

# Back-and-forth between the last two focused spaces (needs SA, same as
# the numbered switches above).
alt - tab : yabai -m space --focus recent

# Move the current space to the next display (explicitly documented as
# needing SA, per `man yabai`).
alt + shift - tab : yabai -m space --display next

# Enter the service submode. 0x29 = kVK_ANSI_Semicolon (the bare ';'
# character can't be used as a literal key here — it's also skhd's own
# mode-transition syntax character, e.g. `key ; mode`).
alt + shift - 0x29 ; service

# ------------------------------------------------------------- service mode
# (aerospace's mode.service.binding)
#
# Deliberate simplification from the AeroSpace original: AeroSpace's service
# actions each auto-return to main mode after firing (single-shot). Chaining
# a self-triggered synthetic escape to replicate that here risks recursing
# into this very binding if escape is ever also bound to a command in this
# mode — not worth it for a convenience. Stay in service mode (like the
# resize mode above) and exit explicitly with escape instead.
service < escape ; default

# Reset the focused space's split ratios to default (closest analog to
# AeroSpace's flatten-workspace-tree "reset layout").
service < r : yabai -m space --equalize

# Toggle the focused window between floating and tiled.
service < f : yabai -m window --toggle float

# Close every window in the current space except the focused one.
service < backspace : yabai -m query --windows --space | /usr/bin/python3 -c "import json,sys,subprocess; w=json.load(sys.stdin); f=[x['id'] for x in w if x['has-focus']]; [subprocess.run(['yabai','-m','window',str(x['id']),'--close']) for x in w if x['id'] not in f]"

service < alt + shift - h : yabai -m window --warp west
service < alt + shift - j : yabai -m window --warp south
service < alt + shift - k : yabai -m window --warp north
service < alt + shift - l : yabai -m window --warp east

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- extra

# Toggle the bar's app-menus swap from the keyboard (YBar-specific, no
# AeroSpace equivalent — "hyper" is skhd's built-in cmd+alt+ctrl+shift alias).
hyper - m : /opt/homebrew/bin/ybar --trigger swap_menus_and_spaces
